Overall altar configuration
Single-altar Bodhisattva-centered composition with one principal deity (Thousand-Armed Guan Yin / 千手千眼觀音) anchoring the visual and hierarchical field. Inner attendant pair flanks the central figure at the same platform tier. A background niche register houses supplementary smaller figures (Buddha/Bodhisattva forms — individual identification not possible from this image). Lower platform tier holds smaller flanking figures, probably protective in function. Forward offering table holds standard offerings (fruit, flowers, incense) and a plaque tentatively reading 福德. Two tall multi-banded vertical elements flank the altar exterior, probably five-coloured ritual pillars.
